    "note": "candidate-001 — first cut of @m0saic/alpine/timeline/v1 (the 8th Alpine template). A vertical milestone timeline in the white card: a spine down a left rail with a dot per event, each event a date + title + description to the right. The spine DRAWS DOWN — each segment + dot cascades in top→bottom with its text fading alongside (reduceMotion → static). Built on the donut/heatmap placeRects model (absolute tight rects on the 4px lattice, grid passed as a full-canvas extraLayer so no insetNode re-quantization). Dots are circles (rounded tiles, no inline-masks); per-event color override supported. Validated valid at 1280x800 (26 sources = 26 frames).",
    "question": "First look at the Alpine timeline. Scrub it — the spine should draw down as the dots + text cascade in. Checking: (1) the spine + dot sizing / the left-rail proportions / dot-to-text gap; (2) the date/title/description type hierarchy + spacing within each event; (3) the draw-down cascade — premium, or too slow/fast? (4) vertical centering + row spacing for 5 events. Open Q: keep description ON by default? I will iterate one nudge at a time.",
